SLH-DSA / SPHINCSLET RTL
  Portions are derived from the SPHINCSLET hardware implementation. The design
  also incorporates third-party SHA-2 components, including Secworks-derived
  SHA-256/SHA-512 RTL. See the original source headers in
  agent/slh_dsa/pristine/ and agent/slh_dsa/slh_src/ for the applicable
  copyright and license terms.

The authors of this repository modified selected files for research on
LLM-guided RTL optimization. Accepted ML-DSA overrides are tracked under
agent/mldsa/mldsa_src/, accepted HQC variants under build/ and agent/hqc/, and
SLH-DSA variants under agent/slh_dsa/. Original copyright and license headers
must be preserved. Dated records of modifications, measurements, negative
results, and superseded results are maintained under docs/findings/.

Additional source headers identify Secworks Sweden AB (SHA-256/SHA-512,
BSD-style two-clause terms), Josh Moles (Keccak, MIT), and Ma'muri (Keccak,
MIT). These notices remain in the affected source files. Apache-2.0 license
text is included in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt. This inventory is not a complete
redistribution clearance; see docs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md for open review items.

The repository-level GPL-3.0 license text does not replace source-specific licenses
or notices attached to third-party files. Users are responsible for reviewing
and complying with all applicable terms before redistribution.

